@startuml seq_flt_shaft_speed_invalid
title SC-FLT-02 - Shaft speed above 8000 rpm: invalid, limp-home, reverse locked out

actor "Console user" as User
participant "Console" as Console
participant "Plant model" as Plant
participant "TCU" as TCU
participant "Red LED\n(TCU board)" as LED

note over User, LED
Covers: SYS-SEN-002, SYS-SEN-001, SYS-FLT-002, SYS-FLT-003, SYS-FLT-004, SYS-FLT-008, SYS-SEL-004, SYS-HMI-001,
SIM-CON-003, SG-01, SG-04
CAN frames pass can0 / slcand / gateway transparently (DC-05, SIM-GW-001), see SC-STA-04.
end note

note over TCU: control active, mode Normal
User -> Console : inject a shaft speed offset (SIM-CON-003)
Console -> Plant : OutputShaftSpeed offset
Plant -> TCU : SIM_Speed: OutputShaftSpeed > 8000 rpm (t0)
TCU -> TCU : value invalid (> 8000 rpm, can_matrix section 3.2): shaft speed invalid fault\n(FaultBits 6, DTC P0715-29) on the first invalid value, no debounce (SYS-SEN-002)
TCU -> TCU : vehicle speed invalid (computed from OutputShaftSpeed, SYS-SEN-001)
TCU -> TCU : enter limp-home, latched (SYS-FLT-002, SYS-FLT-004)
TCU -> Plant : TCU_Actuators: SS_A = OFF, SS_B = OFF, PCS_Duty = 0 %, FaultLamp = ON, RLS = OFF
note right of TCU: <= t0 + 100 ms (SYS-FLT-003)
TCU -> LED : ON (SYS-HMI-001)
TCU -> Plant : TCU_Status: Mode = 1 (Limp-home), VehicleSpeed = 0xFFFF (invalid), FaultBits bit 6 = 1

opt R selected and RLS = ON before the fault
  TCU -> TCU : vehicle speed invalid -> RLS = OFF, also when RLS was ON (SYS-SEL-004)
  Plant -> Plant : RLS = OFF: reverse released, neutral
  note over Plant, TCU: Safe state of SG-01: reverse locked out.
end

note over TCU: an InputShaftSpeed > 8000 rpm sets the same fault;\nthe vehicle speed then stays valid

User -> Console : remove the injection
Plant -> TCU : SIM_Speed: OutputShaftSpeed <= 8000 rpm
TCU -> TCU : the fault stays set until the next power cycle (SYS-FLT-008),\nlimp-home stays latched (SYS-FLT-004)
@enduml
